==Personality==
Looey is a jolly, comical [[Toon]] who's a part of a circus troupe alongside his friends {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} and {{CI|Blot|name=true}}. Though he may be a clown, he knows when things must be taken seriously. Despite being a performer, capable of entertaining live audiences with his hard work, he very ironically seems to have a more shy and nervous side that is most noticeable within his extraction lines and dialogues.

Even more ironically, Looey is hinted to have stage fright, something a performer should not have (his dreams revealing this to {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, him changing the subject when {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} shows interest in watching Looey juggle, and hoping nobody was watching him finish extracting). He also seems to not enjoy being laughed at despite the overall purpose of clowns being to make people laugh at them. His [[Posters|Info card]] either further implies this with the "They're laughing with you" quote, or simply serves as a motivational short speech for the in-universe audience.

As yet another ironic contradiction to his supposed disliking of socializing and general anxiousness, he seems to genuinely enjoy getting along with the other Toons and making sure they're happy. Contradictions aside, he seems to be themed after the trope where a comical character masks their rough inner workings behind a wall of laughter, joy and surprises.

