===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Machine}}|{{MastStrat|second|you can start multiple solo runs and get repeatedly hit by [[Twisteds]] until you die, and then repeat. Let Healer Toons (maybe more than one) like {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} (recommended), {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} (with {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} equipped), or {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} join your run and heal you to be able to get hit again and speed up the time. This strategy helps both yours '''and''' the Healer's masteries (if uncompleted)}}|{{MastStrat|third and fourth|Collect and use|Caps}}|{{MastStrat|fifth|Reach/do floors}}|{{MastStrat|sixth|Meters||Also, get hit twice for the highest Movement Speed possible, though be careful of the Twisteds.}}}}

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, play as {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} and try to complete her [[Mastery]] Quests by going on multiple runs. It is recommended to go on an organized Run or do specific quests in certain runs.

==Strategies==
Looey is an excellent All-Rounded [[Toon]] that can distract or extract. With low [[Stealth]] and a great Passive [[Ability]] that increases his [[Movement Speed]] per lost {{Heart}}, he's excellent at leading [[Twisteds]] around, and his above-average [[Skill Check]] [[Stat]] is helpful for extracting [[Machines]].

His Passive Ability, '''Heart of Helium''', greatly increases distracting capabilities, however, it also increases the risk factor while using him. '''Heart of Helium''' increases his speed by 20% for each [[Heart]] that he's currently missing, allowing him to reach higher speeds than even {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} under certain circumstances. Looey is also faster than average at completing Machines, giving him a great utility on a team even if he plays as a distractor.

On only one Heart, Looey is the fastest Toon in the game and can easily outrun {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} and other fast Twisteds if the player has good [[Trinkets]] in use. The most used Trinket on Looey is {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}, which gives him 10% extra Walk Speed, and even more when paired with {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} (15.5%), {{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}}, or {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}} (both 21% depending on [[Floor]] number). Even without Trinkets, Looey can already out-walk average or slow Twisteds on 2 Hearts, and can almost do the same to every Twisted on one Heart (outside of [[Panic Mode]]) aside from {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}}, enraged {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}} in a [[Blackout]], and Twisted Pebble. However, {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} and her {{Debuff|Slow|II}} could make it a bit harder to distract, especially when on 1 Heart, the exception is if Looey has {{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}} equipped making Twisted Vee more easy to distract on 2 Hearts. Additionally, long-ranged Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}} could be problematic, so it's suggested to have a backup distractor deal with them; if Looey chooses to distract them, {{TI|Cardboard 'Armor'|name=true}} may help if they struggle to distract ranged Twisteds, as his play-style can put him at more risk of death. Do note its single use per Floor though.

Using {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}} or having a {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}} is quite useful, especially if you are a risky player. Despite keeping 2 Hearts being the meta, some people will opt for 1 Heart for ensured out-walking. However, this does make a hit fatal. Savory Charm and Soulvester's Ability aids this, by protecting you from a small mistake, saving you from lag spikes or cornering and also alerting you to be more cautious. Since you'd likely have a far easier time distracting Twisteds like Twisted Pebble and {{CI|Twisted Gourdy|name=true}} with 1 Heart, potentially being able to out-walk some of the fastest Twisteds, having Soulvester constantly guarding you can eliminate the risk of death if you mess up or lag occurs; this is especially good in longer runs due to the increased Main Character Twisted spawn rate. Do realize Savory Charm's one time use and Soulvester's bad survivability and need for Hearts to use the Ability. You'd want a healer on the team if you intend to distract to higher Floors with a Soulvester supporting you.

Looey is a great pick if you're trying to learn to distract Twisteds using Toons with 3{{Star}} Movement Speed. His Ability provides a great buffer against trickier targets, helping you when you're in trouble, and upon being healed the user can return to their learning. His low Stealth greatly aids in keeping Twisteds' attention, which is again, great for beginners. However, compared to {{CI|Goob|name=true}} and other such distractor Toons, Looey carries more risk for more reward—weigh your preferences.

The user might also elect to immediately voluntarily reduce their Hearts to two or even one {{Small|(the prior being preferred)}} for an immediate speed boost, but this effectively turns him into a {{Type|Main}} with one Ability instead of two (or zero if you don't consider the speed boost as a sufficient enough Ability due to it technically accounting for a Main's extra Star). Still, even this method has unique Stats to offer compared to other Toons, so it's not beyond consideration—just be sure to trust your skill level before trying. If you elect to aim for 3 Hearts, Looey still makes a great back-up distractor and can extract during downtime, especially if a healer like {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} is in your party.

Speaking of healers, be sure to communicate with teammates what your preferred heart total is, as everyone has their own ideal amount. Even if your party lacks a healer, let others know ahead of time; You may end up wasting a heal [[Card]] if they worry for you, or worse, avoiding a needed heal because they assume you prefer low HP. Looey has a harder time sustaining health than other Distractors due to his Ability—heal Cards are often wasted, half of a {{II|Health Kit|name=true}}'s value must be sacrificed to retain 2 Hearts status, and occasionally Looey will take intentional damage to deal with tough Twisteds, needing to use additional healing to regain a safe HP level.

As an extractor, Looey can extract most Machines at an above average pace, and if injured, he can additionally extract Treadmill Machines fairly quickly. You can purposefully get hit during Panic Mode when everyone else is in the Elevator, or get hit by certain Twisted like {{CI|Twisted Squirm|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Blot|name=true}}, if you want to have a consistent higher speed. Take note of your Stealth as it can make it easier for other teammates to swap Twisted aggro onto you, or risk getting in the way of distractors. Since without speed Trinkets Looey can still reach a high enough Movement Speed to outspeed various Twisteds, you can help gather Twisteds for a distractor and protect teammates, though only if you know what you're doing–you could end up causing problems or accidentally sabotaging teammates.

The best [[Items]] to look out for as a distractor are mobility Items and healing Items. Movement Speed Items can stack with Looey's speed boost and temporarily let you regenerate Stamina in preparation for Panic Mode or changing your distracting location. Stamina Items can help you keep your Stamina up, something important considering the risk involved with having less Hearts. Healing Items will ensure you stay alive, though you should usually focus on having at least 1 {{II|Bandage|name=false}}, since you can better control your speed, while also not wasting the value. When extracting, Looey can make good use of Items like {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}} owing to his high Skill Check Stat, though Items like {{II|Instructions|name=false}} are still very useful for completing Machines faster. You can also use speed or Stamina related Items for Treadmill Machines though only if they're more common, as it could end up being a waste otherwise.

Overall, Looey is an excellent Toon to play as, with distraction being his best occupation, reaching higher speeds, though depleted Health makes him a high-risk-high-reward Toon. Even so, his decent extraction keeps him as a solid Toon, especially when it comes to Treadmill Machines.

