==Trivia==
*Looey is the only [[Toon]] to have their [[Introduction Card]] have a quote and to be made up of two bodies of text.
*Looey's head will be shrunken if you are on 2{{Heart}}, and even more if 1 Heart. During then, his ears cartoonishly disconnect from his head.
**However, the ears disconnecting could just be a modeling error.
*Looey on 1 [[Heart]] with the [[Movement Speed]] buff from {{TI|Lucky Coin|name=true}} and {{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}} or {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}} gives a Run Speed multiplier of 72.48%, which gives a Run Speed of 43.12, making him the fastest [[Toon]] in the game without any [[Items]] and/or supports.
**When given 3 {{II|Jawbreaker|name=true}}s with the Movement Speed buff and 7 of {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}'s [[Ability]], you would get a theoretical Run Speed multiplier of 2675.76%, which gives a run speed of 668.94.
*Previously, his [[Ability]] was intended to increase 1{{Star}} for [[Movement Speed]] (2.5 units) for each missing [[Heart]], but a bug caused Looey to increase Movement Speed by 20% (3 units for Walk Speed and 5 units for Run Speed). The Ability's description was later changed, making it an actual feature. This makes him faster than {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} (on odd floors) at 1 Heart.
**If their Ability did add 1 Star for each missing Heart (in percentage values), at 2 Hearts their Movement Speed would need to be increased by ≈16.67% (Walk Speed) and 10% (Run Speed). While at 1 Hearts his Movement Speed would need to be increased by ≈33.34% (Walk Speed) and 20% (Run Speed).
*Looey was the hardest character to balance; figuring out how much speed Looey would get after getting hit was the most challenging part. It would get to the point where it would be impossible for any [[Twisted]] to damage him.<ref>https://youtu.be/KctAr8qwcSU&t=1107 (18:27)</ref>
*Looey and {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} are friends.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1314757242465026139</ref> Poppy's [[Mastery]] being needed to unlock Looey, their Passive [[Abilities]] similarities (Movement Speed boosts from taking damage), their material similarities (pop-able balls), and the fact one of their interactions is nothing but them repeatedly saying "pop" can also reflect this.
*Looey is part of the '''Circus Troupe''' with {{CI|Blot|name=true}} and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}. He takes on the role of a clown and the leader, but he ironically seems to not want to be the leader, despite him being one in the [[Show]]. When he attempts to employ {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} as a fourth member of the circus, it could be likely that Looey was actually trying to get Flyte to replace him.
**Additionally, he tells {{CI|Astro|name=true}} that he has stage fright, something state performers should not have (or at least have overcome), maybe due to others laughing at him (despite that being a clown's role).
