*Looey hinted to [[Blot]] being a mime, as seen in an interaction with [[Teagan]].
*Looey is slightly different compared to the other Circus Troupe members.
**He was released with [[Connie]], not alone.
**The update he was released in didn't revamp any maps.
**He wasn't released in 2025.
**He never showed up in the game's icon in the update he released in.
**He doesn't show up on any visible banners for the game's page.
***Therefore, he doesn't show up with any form of [[Razzle & Dazzle]] in the banners.
**He doesn't have 3 requirements.
**His [[Mastery]] doesn't require another [[Toon]] to be played with.
**He didn't receive a new [[Skin]] from Dandy's Store on the v0.10 update.
**He doesn't have 4 Star Movement Speed.
**He doesn't have a unique number of Stars in each of his [[Stats]].
***One could argue that Looey gains 4 Star Speed at 2 Hearts and 5 Star Speed at one. However, it is just a multiplier and therefore doesn't count. Plus, he is slightly faster at 2 Hearts compared to 4 Star Movement Speed and also a bit faster at 1 Heart compared to 5 Star Movement Speed.
*Looey is one of the first non-[[Main]] [[Toons]] to get a [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]] with the other Toons being [[Blot]], [[Razzle & Dazzle]] and [[Yatta]] with the [[Show-Time Cosmetic Pack]].
*When the "Astro in Stage Fright" [[Poster]] was updated, Looey was added in the audience, though only one of his ears is visible.
*Looey shares the same [[Stats]] as {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, making this the second instance 2 [[Toons]] shared the same Stats and didn't have base Stats; {{CI|Coal|name=true}} and [[Flutter]] are the first instance.
*There is an error in Looey's "{{SI|Good Job|name=true}}" [[Sticker]], where his right hand is yellow instead of purple.
*Looey and {{CI|Boxten|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] to be able to have permanent, though situational [[Multipliers|boosts]] in an entire run, with Boxten's [[Extraction Speed]] Boost per person and Looey's [[Movement Speed]] buff per hit.
*The [[Easter Event]] is the only [[Event]] to immediately release Looey's Event [[Skin]]; the rest released them in a later patch.
*[[Skins]] starting from Creepy Clown onward have Looey not slightly floating on his animations. This is most likely an animation correction, making his knees properly bend.
*According to New York Comic Con art and his {{CI|Twisted Looey}}[[Twisted Looey|Twisted counterpart]], Looey's head is connected to his body through a string and his head can be disconnected from his body.
*Looey is the last base-game {{Type|Common}} [[Toon]] to be in 2024.
**He and [[Connie]] are the last Toons to be added in [[Dandy's Store]] in 2024.

